    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## RM: Publish ready posts to Instagram\n\n**Starts:** daily 08:00.\n\nTakes the **oldest** `ready_to_post` row from `content_queue`, posts it, and marks the row. One post a\nday, never a backlog dump.\n\nInstagram's API is two steps: create a media container, wait for it to finish, then publish it. The\nwait is not optional \u2014 publishing too early fails.\n\nA failed post marks the row rather than losing it, so it can be retried deliberately.",
        "height": 286,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "overview-note",
      "name": "What this workflow does",
